[Term]
id: UBERON:0006777
name: tectal plate
def: "Embryologic structure that is formed by two longitudinal eminences, one on each alar plate of the midbrain. These eminences become the superior colliculus and inferior colliculus ( Carpenter-1983 )]." [http://braininfo.rprc.washington.edu/centraldirectory.aspx?type=a&ID=453]
comment: The term "tectal plate" (or "quadrigeminal plate") is used to describe the junction of the gray and white matter in the embryo. (NeuroNames ancil-453)
synonym: "lamina quadrigemina" EXACT OMO:0003011 [FMA:77488, FMA:TA]
synonym: "quadrigeminal plate" EXACT [FMA:77488]
