[Term]
id: UBERON:0034751
name: primary auditory cortex
def: "The part of the auditory cortex that is located on the superior temporal gyrus in the temporal lobe and receives point-to-point input from the ventral division of the medial geniculate complex." [http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK10900/]
synonym: "A1C" RELATED OMO:0003000 [DHBA:10236]
synonym: "auditory complex area A1" RELATED [NCBIBook:NBK10900]
