[Term]
id: UBERON:0034754
name: occipitofrontal fasciculus
def: "The occipitofrontal fasciculus passes backward from the frontal lobe, along the lateral border of the caudate nucleus, and on the medial aspect of the corona radiata; its fibers radiate in a fan-like manner and pass into the occipital and temporal lobes lateral to the posterior and inferior cornua." [Wikipedia:Occipitofrontal_fasciculus]
synonym: "inferior occipitofrontal fasciculus" RELATED [Wikipedia:Occipitofrontal_fasciculus]
synonym: "off" RELATED OMO:0003000 [DHBA:10588]
